-- title:
--   Constant residues and node generators for the local ring at x
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring such that for all $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b\neq 0$ one has $b\mid a^{n}$ for some $n$. Let $F/L$ be a field which is a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, all places have residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type over $L$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally of finite presentation morphism $\mathrm{toBase}:X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, all of whose stalks are integrally closed, together with a ring isomorphism $\varphi:F\cong K(X)$ carrying the constants $a\in A$ to their images under the structure morphism. Let $A_0$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi_0$, and $\iota_0:A_0\to A$ an injective local homomorphism inducing a surjection on residue fields and such that every $a\in A$ is algebraic over the subring $\iota_0(A_0)$; let $X_0\to\operatorname{Spec}A_0$ be integral, proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, and let an isomorphism $X\cong X_0\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A_0}\operatorname{Spec}A$ be given compatibly with the structure morphisms. Fix a point $x\in X$ lying over the closed point of $A$, closed for specialisation, and exactly two further points $\eta_1\neq\eta_2$ specialising to $x$, distinct from $x$ and lying over the closed point (any such point is $\eta_1$ or $\eta_2$), whose local rings in $F$ are the valuation rings of regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to $F$ with residue fields $\bar F_1,\bar F_2$. Let $x_0\in X_0$ be the image of $x$, let $w\geq 1$ be invertible in $A_0$, and assume a ring isomorphism between the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}$ and the crossing model $\widehat A_0[[u,v]]/(uv-\varpi_0^{\,w})$ sending each $a\in A_0$ to the constant class of $a$. Let $\mathcal N_0\subseteq F$ be a local Noetherian subring with a ring isomorphism $\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}\cong\mathcal N_0$ realised by the stalk map to $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ followed by $\varphi^{-1}$, with $\mathcal N_0$ contained in $\mathcal N:=\varphi^{-1}(\mathcal O_{X,x})\subseteq F$, and assume every constant $a\in A$ lies in $\mathcal N$. Finally let $x_n,y_n,t\in\mathcal N_0$ with $t$ the constant $\iota_0(\varpi_0)$ and $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal N_0}=(x_n,y_n,t)$. The conclusion is twofold: first, for every $q\in\mathcal N$ there is $a\in A$ with $q-a$ a non-unit of $\mathcal N$; second, every non-unit $q\in\mathcal N$ can be written $q=x_n\alpha+y_n\beta+t\gamma+p\,\delta$ with $\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta\in\mathcal N$ and $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This identifies the local ring of a proper flat normal model at an ordinary double point descended from a henselian discrete valuation base: its residue field is generated by the constants from $A$, and its maximal ideal is generated by the two node coordinates, the descended uniformiser and the maximal ideal of $A$. It is the glue step used by [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_nodeRing_coords_and_branch_unique_and_residue_surjective_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_of_isUnit_of_isIntegrallyClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_nodeRing_coords_and_branch_unique_and_residue_surjective_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_of_isUnit_of_isIntegrallyClosed) in the analysis of nodes of semistable models.
